Counting: `counts[w] = counts.GetValueOrDefault(w) + 1;`. A `Dictionary` doesn't promise any order; `SortedDictionary` keeps keys sorted. In games: item name → count in an inventory, enemy type → stats.

example.code:
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        var totals = new SortedDictionary<string, int>();
        foreach (var (crop, kg) in new[] { ("maize", 40), ("beans", 12), ("maize", 25) })
            totals[crop] = totals.GetValueOrDefault(crop) + kg;
        foreach (var (crop, kg) in totals) Console.WriteLine($"{crop}: {kg} kg");
    }
}

